exclude.description:
An expression in VRL to exclude certain operations from being sent to Hive Console.
Returning `true` from this expression will exclude the operation, while `false` will include it.
This expression is a VRL expression that has access to the request and operation details;

```vrl
 if (.request.operation.name == "ExcludeMe") {
   true
 } else {
   false
 }
```
Backward compatible with both:
- an expression object: `{ expression: "..." }`
- a list of operation names

oneOf.description:
Accept headers from the `headers` field from the GraphQL operation extensions.

For example, if the connected client sends a GraphQL operation like:

```json
{
  "query": "{ topProducts { name } }",
  "extensions": {
    "headers": {
      "Authorization": "Bearer abc123"
    }
  }
}
```

The headers will be extracted and considered for the subgraph respecting the header
propagation rules as well as validating against any JWT rules defined in the configuration.

